From 6dfb0e30ef5cf23239fa8ecb05edf0ccee4aa50b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zabeelbasheer <53309631+zabeelbasheer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:56:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat: phase 4, PDF export and cross-audit checklist page

PDF report: real reportlab Platypus document, branded (navy/gold/
parchment palette), grouped by NIST function, critical items called
out separately, action items table at the end. Two real bugs caught
by actually rendering and inspecting the output at 200 DPI, not just
checking it built without erroring: a ParagraphStyle for the 26pt
score number had no explicit leading, defaulting to a value tuned for
10pt text, which visually cut a line through the score; isolated with
a minimal two-paragraph test before touching the real fix. And a
warning-sign unicode glyph in the critical blockers header rendered as
a black box, Helvetica base font does not have that character,
replaced with plain bold red text. Verified again against a full
24-criterion dataset for pagination and text wrapping, and against the
real PDF endpoint end to end, confirmed as a genuine valid PDF file
via the file command, not just a byte count.

Cross-audit checklist page: new get_all_checklist_items() joins through
audit_sessions for ownership scoping, aggregating every action item
across every audit rather than requiring a click into each one. Inline
editable owner, due date, and status, PATCH per field on blur/change.
Tested end to end against a running server: list returns the right
joined data, update persists, immediately reflected on re-fetch.

Also fixes an in_progress.title() bug that rendered as In_Progress
in the PDF, found while testing realistic status values.

One process note: hit the exact background-process-across-separate-
tool-calls trap from earlier tonight while testing this, boot and
requests split across two calls silently no-op instead of erroring,
looked like a checklist bug until isolated back to that.
